Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Stdio Host P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] 9d54c05a-cc11-4851-bf9f-08958e93d0bf
@ [specification_uuid] 4ee53d21-ed53-4f35-bbaf-06cab3a34085

& [Executable]
  + one cantor-sop-inspect-stdio binary target depends only on std and cantor_sop_inspect_wire
  + main returns an exact internal disposition converted at the outermost edge to process exit

& [Admission]
  + reject nonzero argument count before touching stdin
  + read fixed chunks into a vector capped at MAX_WIRE_REQUEST_BYTES plus one and require EOF plus nonempty content
  + do not parse dispatch or echo before admission completes

& [Execution]
  + call cantor_sop_inspect_wire respond exactly once
  + treat Ok bytes including a nested refused status as transportable response truth
  + map Err to the fixed public host fault without serializing the error

& [Publication]
  + write_all exact response bytes and flush stdout
  + before output begins a host failure may write the fixed ASCII stderr code; once output is attempted only exit failure remains legal
  + success is legal only after complete write and flush

& [BoundsAndEffects]
  + stdin bytes are capped by MAX_WIRE_REQUEST_BYTES plus one and stdout by the wire response bound
  + stderr is one constant under128 bytes
  + exact effect accounts are stdin_reads at most one admitted stream stdout_responses zero-or-one stderr_faults zero-or-one semantic_dispatches zero-or-one and all non-stdio effects zero

& [Verification]
  + direct library response and fresh-process stdout must be byte-identical
  + adversarial tests prove pre-dispatch refusals non-echoing behavior mutual exclusivity and deterministic exits
  + static tests reject filesystem network environment shell service provider model and child-process imports
